PREFIX: TC-H1FWT-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-15
TITLE: Timer Characteristics 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user runs a treatment plan for 121 seconds, make sure the timers can handle 
the timing of 2 minutes without any issues even though with a special version of firmware 
application that doesn’t stop the treatment.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run about 2 minutes 
* The system is ready to run without any issues. 
* Load a firmware application that doesn’t stop the treatment.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start a run for the loaded treatment plan for 121 seconds.
2. Check the timers on GUI
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started without any issues. 
2. Verify the timers can handle about 2 minutes treatment without any issues.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-10
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-16
TITLE: Timer Functionality 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
If a user reset the timers in the middle of emission, verify the emission finishes as normal and basically resetting the timers doesn’t effect on emission. Also, the timers won’t count down.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to use and run a loaded treatment plan
2. A treatment plan is loaded into the system.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. After 5 seconds of emission, reset the timers through the screen by clicking reset timer button.
3. Check the ongoing emission process
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the timers are resetting
3. Verify that the emission finishes as normal without the timers resetting. Also, the timers won’t countdown if the system is running.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-2
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-17
TITLE: Timer Functionality 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system starts and finishes an emission, resetting the timers will set the timers to 0
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
2. The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. Wait till the emission is done without any issues.
3. Click the Reset Timer button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the system’s state went back to ready. Also, verify that the timer values are within 20 seconds +/- 10%.
3. Verify that the timers reset, and their values are 0
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-18
TITLE: Communication 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
Req:

The firmware shall verify a checksum value to ensure valid communication with the main control microcontroller
Methode:

The tester will load a variant of Main Control FW where the checksum is corrupt. The timer will generate a fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. Main Control FW variant <#TIMER_COMM_TEST_2_MODE> is loaded
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Prepare a treatment plan on the internal application:
• Energy: 50kV
• Dwell time: 20 sec
• Collimator: any
• Pixels: any

2. Load the treatment plan
to the external application

3. Execute the treatment
plan
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Emission won’t start and
timer checksum fault will
appear
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-5
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-19
TITLE: Communication 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When a user starts an emission, the timers will start to increase.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
